# Check everything out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git hands Windows a CRLF working tree. A test that reads a
# repo file and matches against '\n' then finds nothing there and nowhere
# else — which is exactly what happened to test/readme-is-executable.ts, and
# it only surfaced because that test asserts it found something.
#
# Node tooling reads LF fine on Windows, so there is nothing to trade away.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
